      {
        "id": 131760,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-17T20:37:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Because it doesn't say \"use another power now.\" Just \"use an additional power this turn.\" Seems like you'd do that on your power phase, or at least have the option to choose at the very least.</p><blockquote><p>If the card granting an additional power use is played on the card's owner's turn, <strong>before</strong> the use power phase,&nbsp;then must wait until their use power phase to use the additional power. (this is the typical use case, BTW)</p></blockquote><p>That basically confirms it, then. Right? Fanatic plays Smite the Transgressor during her turn, plays another card from Pillars of Hercules, and then up to three powers due to Hercules and Transgressor, on her power phase only.</p><p>...right?</p>",
